Literal independent toy oracles
-------------------------------

All permutations act on row-basis vectors on the RIGHT. Embed permutations
of positions0..5 in7x7 permutation matrices, fixing coordinate6. These are
Original-free test matrices; no claim that they are natural G2 members.

Let a=(0 1), b=(1 2), c=(2 3), H=<a,b,c>=S4 on0..3, v=e0. The exact
vector orbit has4 elements, stabilizer size6, |H|=24.

* Omitted x=(4 5) fixes v, so v*x is in the orbit, but x is not in H.
  The full matrix coset check must return False. Orbit preservation alone
  is not the expected test. This also satisfies distant commuting relations.
* Kernel-only positive x=(0 1)(2 3) is in H and must return True.
  It is deliberately not a complete rank-four string-admission fixture.
* For a full four-distinct/string positive fixture take c'=(2 3)(4 5),
  H'=<a,b,c'>. Since (b*c')^3=(4 5), H'=S4 x C2, of order48. For v=e0
  the orbit has4 elements, stabilizer size12. Omitted e=(4 5) is in H'
  and commutes with a,b. The four marks are distinct nonidentity involutions
  and all required distant relations hold. This is a toy scope only.

For an independent LEFT-factor orientation oracle let T2=a*b. Its action
on coordinates0..6 is (2,0,1,3,4,5,6). For the edge labelled a at node2:

    T2*a = b*T2 = (2,1,0,3,4,5,6),
    T2*b = (1,0,2,3,4,5,6).

Thus b*T2 is the correct left factor and T2*b is wrong. Use these literal
expected tuples, not recomputation of the same expression as its oracle.
The distinction survives replacing c by c'. Every edge must ultimately
compare all49 matrix entries; the seed image alone is not its authority.

Compact meaningful control groups
---------------------------------

These are advisory groups, to be merged with the author's existing designs;
this document does not prescribe an executed count or retag old controls.

1. Exact toy sizes/order and omitted membership: S4(4,6,24), same-orbit
   omittedFalse; H'(4,12,48), omittedTrue. Assert all endpoint/GEN/IP/paid
   credit flags remain false in the numerical fact/proposal layer.
2. Literal left-factor orientation oracle above; a syntax-valid mutation
   of an actual edge target/stabilizer index, including the LAST full edge,
   must fail the complete equation rather than a decoder shape predicate.
3. Root/parent-tree integrity: duplicate orbit row; a non-earlier parent;
   wrong parent label; out-of-range target; corrupt actual Schreier generator
   edge id; duplicate generator ids; malformed unique roots; trailing bytes.
4. Stabilizer proof: wrong stabilizer multiplication target at the last
   table entry; duplicate stabilizer matrix; a purported element not fixing
   seed; disconnected parent expression; k=0,m>1. Do not replace the genuine
   H-word provenance with a supplied order or an unverified independent S.
5. Finite caps: ncap3 on the4-point orbit and scap5 on the6-element seed
   stabilizer must stop inconclusively, not yield partial certificates/order.
   Separate malformed-cap Boolean/negative/enlarged inputs must refuse.
6. Shared work accounting: one tuple multiply then one byte multiply uses
   the SAME product bank; one tuple row image then one byte row image uses
   the SAME row bank. Start at the boundary so the second debit refuses.
   Scalar and IO/closing rereads must consume the same persistent banks;
   never reset on a per-case, producer-recheck or conversion boundary.
7. Supplied-only independence: checker must not call build, small_closure,
   seed search, prime_value or fixed_basis. Bind the supplied carrier and
   exact current three ordered marks/omitted fourth. A malformed supplied
   certificate refuses; it must not trigger reconstruction or repair.
8. Typed/scope admission: wrong job/position/endpoint/order/frame/paid
   status/reviewer/import/gate schema, Boolean identity or cap substitution,
   wrong Source/control subject, obsolete selector and false Root ownership
   refuse. Synthetic metadata fixtures remain explicit in-memory doubles,
   not fabricated actual SDKs or real positive Root authority documents.
9. Publication boundary: mid-build, mid-check/member and pre-publication
   work stops must not publish a partial positive carrier/fact. Function-only
   stop controls cannot claim an observed guard/filesystem absence event.
   Distinguish well-formed omittedFalse, malformed refusal and resource stop.

Adapter and resource pitfalls for the frozen Source read
--------------------------------------------------------

* PS tuple image uses self.row_images, while the old byte image uses
  self.rows. They MUST alias one row bank. A clearly documented property
  alias can preserve the old byte method literally; separate attributes
  silently double capacity. Both multiply implementations already use
  self.products. The actual counter fields and emitted counts must agree.
* Dynamic dispatch must retain exact bytes versus tuple result types;
  field.I is49 bytes while context I7 is a tuple of rows. Conversions are
  typed/canonical/charged and are not a second independent work bank.
* The override tick must apply the stricter90s/112MiB cooperative envelope
  to inherited context/tuple IO as well as the byte operations. Keep the
  old100s/128MiB declared role and old c3b/5c7 outer profile exact. Earlier
  125s PS timing is ancestry, not a new relaxed active limit.
* Public encode and decode each debit carrier length to the200000 linear
  bank. At the maximum121315-byte extent, doing BOTH in one role alone
  exceeds that bank. This is not a mathematical flaw if the role stops
  honestly, but do not promise all NMAX carriers can complete or hide the
  second debit. Context/validation/check/member consume this same bank.
* Exact loaded public whole bodies and the new tiny runtime shim have a
  new Source subject. Prevent cached/unpinned import substitution before
  any project function use; -B alone does not disable cached-bytecode reads.
